{
  "requirement": "The `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents not to commit requirements or write implementation or test code until the user has agreed to, rejected, or deferred every group.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement has one obligation. The bundled `habeas-requirements` skill must direct agents not to commit requirements, and not to write implementation or test code, until the user has agreed to, rejected, or deferred every group.\n\n`tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_requirements_skill_gates_commit_and_code_on_every_group_being_decided]` carries the `{test}` reference. It calls `assert_phrases(\"habeas-requirements\", …)` with the full gate sentence: \"**Gate:** no implementation or test code, and no commit, until the user has agreed to, rejected, or deferred every group\". The helper reads the bundled skill through `bundled_skill`. `bundled_skill` collapses whitespace over `SKILL.md` and its reference files, and `assert_text` asserts the phrase is contained. I did not read `collapse` itself. The skill's gate text is hard-wrapped across lines, so the assertion only holds if `collapse` joins wrapped lines, and I am assuming it does. The sentence covers every clause of the requirement:\n- implementation code and test code;\n- commits;\n- the three accepted outcomes (agreed, rejected, deferred);\n- the scope \"every group\".\n\nDropping the commit gate, dropping the code gate, narrowing \"every group\" to some groups, or dropping an outcome would all break the phrase match and fail the test.\n\nOther tests in the same file add checks that do not substitute for this one. `the_requirements_skill_commits_agreed_requirements_before_code` and `the_requirements_skill_commits_every_group_together_before_code` check where the gate sits relative to the commit step. `the_requirements_skill_is_home_of_drafting_review_references_and_criteria` checks that the gate marker exists.\n\nThe assertion is a literal-phrase check. That suits a requirement about what a skill document says, and no other tested input class or boundary affects the obligation. I found no gap and no `{fixme}` acknowledgments.",
